                        "Name": "Electrical Properties",
                        "Description": "Measurements of the electrical properties of rock provide fundamental input to calibrate and interpret resistivity log measurements for water saturation interpretation. The primary electrical property tests are: formation resistivity factor (F or FRF), resistivity index (I) and cation-exchange capacity tests (wet chemistry CEC and multiple salinity Qv methods). These data are applied in fluid saturation models.",
